  "texts": [
    "An induction hob boils water, yet makes no heat itself. How?",
    "Under the glass hides a copper coil.",
    "Alternating current flips direction tens of thousands of times a second.",
    "The current creates a magnetic field that keeps changing.",
    "The field passes through the glass into the pot's bottom.",
    "A changing field induces electric current in the metal.",
    "These eddy currents swirl in circles inside the pot.",
    "The metal resists the current, turning its energy into heat.",
    "So the pot itself is the heater, not the hob.",
    "The glass only gets warm from the hot pot.",
    "It works best with a magnetic pot, test it with a magnet.",
    "Aluminum or glass pots won't heat on most hobs.",
    "About ninety percent of the energy reaches the food, gas only forty.",
    "Lift the pot and the hob switches off the field.",
    "Follow for more kitchen physics!"
  ]
